## Side-by-side self-check (per chapter, after the probe)

I listed every manuscript sentence matching a source sentence at ≥0.40 and read each pair against the source passage it came from, asking whether the passage kept a source sentence's beats in the source's order. What I found and rebuilt (always from the event list, with a new device or order — no synonym swaps, no splits):

- **ch21 (first draft 4% / 18%):** Karis's "other column" followed the source's *X did Y because Z* list in the same order → rebuilt as texts named, each with what it did, nearest first; Lira's "if the archive's wrong" → "his letter was true" exchange (Brom asks); "counted the room" tally → a new tally (firewood table, sixty days, a fortnight); the carters' "nobody asks your tier" → *Nobody's got a book to write you in*; Karis's papers face down → turned to the slate wall "as if it were a guest". Final 0% / 10%.
- **ch22 (first draft heavy — the dairy argument tracked the source's sequence most closely):** Brom's three sentences recast ("Win the sittings. Keep a box."); his box contents and "not much for a box"; Cael's receipts reordered from Denvash forward, Umber named, the "text held / true record on a counter" sentences replaced; Lira's "It's working now?" removed (Cael pre-empts the objection); Brom's "if the code doesn't have one" removed; Karis's induction re-said ("Every rule anybody ever broke looked exactly like this the evening before"); Lira's Fenmark details and "check the ground" → joists and "look underneath"; the tea finding, lamp, and "in four months… the night we decided" → the slow kettle, counting cups, "Memory improves things"; Seln's window posting list, "who decided… since when", the column-of-the-circle list (it mirrored the source's girl/researcher/big one/boy order) → the dairy step and the lamp he held; "arguing with a malfunction" dropped as a sentence. Final 2% / 14% (the 2% is the two packet lines).
- **ch23:** Rooke's "everything built for the second exchange / program or decoration" and "only number that matters" → recomposed; the four-minute brief line recast. Final 0% / 12%.
- **ch24 (bout):** E2's "made him choose between finishing a course and covering" mechanism replaced by a new one (she stands on the course before its fourth count — "a promise broken before it's kept"); E3's "he gave up the centre, read half a beat late as generosity" replaced by the fan that walks her like a raft; E4's "at range, declining to be interesting" replaced by the Silver standing on his kept courses; "fighting the file / the woman" and the bill's bruise sentence recomposed; "long and low" ovation recast. Final 0% / 5%.
- **ch25:** "what it cost to be seen cheering" → applause "taken back… to weigh"; the two-papers look before "Noted" and the folding-as-goodbye ending both mirrored the source's order → rebuilt (she holds her sheet up beside his; the folds won't lie the same way twice; it will go in the box). Final 1% / 11%.
- **ch26 (first draft tracked badly in two places):** the interrogatory's *wave down the benches → clerk's pen → Ilsev looks up* and *Jent did not consult / did not ask to answer in writing* followed the source's beats in order → rebuilt as Ilsev first, then the clerk, then forty benches where not one pencil moves, with Jent on his feet "before the breath was finished"; Cael's reflection (corridor / two lines / fifteen years / courtesy / cost him nothing) was a near paraphrase → **redrafted whole** around his dairy notes being evidence; the steps scene (Karis on what Jent could have said; "most frightening sentence") was a near paraphrase → **redrafted whole** ("Did you hear what he called me?"; "He wasn't even careful"); Karis writing it in the front matter → the card into the front cover in the coach. The gate: the lodge board's lines, Withrow's read-aloud reason, the gallery as "furniture", the word count and "man on a horse", Bracken's seal routine and his "seal is a claim / place this one" lines all tracked → rebuilt (a new board; "My lodge-man… has never once heard one read"; behind the bell-frame; the name at the top; deckle, glass, then his thumb with eyes shut; "I can't write four riders in it"). Final 2% / 15% (the 2% is the escort order and the question).
- **ch27 (first draft heaviest of the movement, ~40 pairs ≥0.42):** the rider's offer, Withrow's answer, the exits list, Withrow's log instruction, the rumour sequence, the "price" paragraph, Gault's steadying sentence, the notebook's Shield comparison and "two tests", Seln's Anchor speech (its no-champions / no-bracket / service-takes-them order was the source's), the grade line, Karis's "thin" paragraph and Lira's question all tracked → each rebuilt (e.g. Seln now speaks from posting rolls and the service's letter to the family; Karis's "a registrar who reads seals with his thumb… how little of it there was"; the notebook's horse trained too). Final 1% / 18%.
- **Honest note:** the close band in ch27 (18%) is the movement's highest; I read its 0.35–0.45 pairs and what remains is event-level overlap (a refusal, a query, a rumour, the Anchor name) in different words and order. The first drafts of ch22, ch26 and ch27 tracked despite drafting with the source closed — the cause was memory of a single strong read of tightly built source scenes (the council's speech order; the interrogatory; the gate). The rebuilds changed entry points and devices, not only words.

